  "rulesTitle": "Rules summary",
  "rulesMenuHint": "The most important scoring rules, by expansion.",
  "rulesBase": "• City: completed gives 2 pts per tile and pennant, unfinished (at the end of the game) 1 pt.\n• Road: 1 pt per tile, completed or not.\n• Cloister: completed 9 pts (the cloister and 8 tiles around it), unfinished 1 pt per tile including the cloister.\n• Farms: at the end of the game 3 pts for each completed city next to the farm.\n• Points go to the player with the most meeples; on a tie every tied player gets the full points.\n• The score during the game is the points from the board. The goods bonus and the value of gold are added only in the final summary.",
  "rulesInns": "• Cathedral: a completed city with a cathedral gives 3 pts per tile and pennant, an unfinished one 0 pts.\n• Inn: a completed road with an inn gives 2 pts per tile, an unfinished one 0 pts.\n• A big meeple counts as two meeples for the majority, but does not double the points.",
  "rulesTraders": "• Goods: a completed city with a symbol gives a wine, grain or cloth token (to the player who completed the city).\n• At the end of the game, for each kind of goods the player with the most tokens gets 10 pts (on a tie each gets 10 pts).\n• Pig: with a pig each completed city next to the farm gives 4 pts instead of 3.\n• The builder and the pig do not count for the majority.",
  "rulesPrincess": "• Fairy: at the start of your turn you get 1 pt if the fairy stands next to your meeple.\n• When a feature with a meeple next to the fairy is scored, its owner gets an extra 3 pts, also at the end of the game.\n• The dragon and the princess do not change scoring in the app.",
  "rulesTower": "• The ransom for a captured meeple is 3 pts, which go to the player holding the prisoner. Also 3 pts for a big meeple.\n• You can buy back a meeple, a big meeple, a wagon and a mayor. Builders and pigs cannot be captured.\n• You buy back on your own turn, once per turn. Without 3 points you cannot buy a meeple back.\n• A meeple-for-meeple swap (two players hold each other prisoners) happens automatically, without points and without the app.",
  "rulesAbbey": "• The abbey scores like a cloister: completed 9 pts, unfinished 1 pt per tile.\n• Barn, normal farm scoring: 3 pts per city.\n• A farm joined to a barn: farmers get 1 pt per city (2 with a pig), 2 pts per castle.\n• The barn owner at the end of the game: 4 pts per city and 5 per castle, no pig.",
  "rulesBridges": "• Castle: its owner gets the points of the completed city, road or cloister it stands next to. A castle does not score at the end of the game.\n• A castle on a farm is worth 4 pts instead of 3 (5 with a pig).\n• Bazaar: the player who picked the tile buys it from the highest bidder (pays them the price) or sells it to them (receives the price). If only they bid, they pay the price and nobody gains.\n• Bridges do not change scoring.",
  "rulesHills": "• Vineyards: a completed cloister gets 3 pts for each vineyard on the tiles around it.\n• Sheep: a flock of 1–4 sheep tokens, every shepherd on the farm gets points for the whole flock. A wolf scatters the flock. Sheep do not score at the end of the game.",
  "rulesCircus": "• Circus: reveal an animal token. Every meeple on the circus tile and the eight neighboring ones gives its owner as many points as the animal is worth (elephant 7, lion 6, bear 5, seal 4, monkey 3, flea 1). The meeples stay.\n• Acrobats: a completed pyramid (3 meeples) – each acrobat 5 pts and returns to the supply. At the end of the game 5 pts for each acrobat on the board.\n• Ringmaster: 2 pts for each circus or acrobat tile next to him, also at the end of the game.",
  "rulesGold": "• Gold: 16 bars. For a completed feature the bars on its tiles go to the player with the majority (not to farmers).\n• At the end of the game a bar is worth: 1–3 bars 1 pt each, 4–6 2 pts, 7–9 3 pts, 10+ 4 pts.",
  "gameStartedTitle": "The game has started!",
  "noPlayersHint2": "To edit a player, press and hold their row.",
  "summaryTitle": "Summary",
  "modifyExpansions": "Modify expansions",
  "backToEdit": "Back to editing players",
