  "expMonasteries": "German and Dutch monasteries",
  "expMonasteriesDesc": "Monasteries with an abbot who stays until the end of the game and scores along lines: 1 pt for each tile in the monastery row and column plus 1 pt for the monastery itself. A monastery with a monk scores like a normal cloister.",
  "scMonastery": "Abbot",
  "monasteryPointsLabel": "Abbot end-game points",
  "monasteryHint": "Enter the abbot end-game points: 1 pt for each tile in the monastery row and column (counted from the monastery up to the first gap in each direction) and 1 pt for the monastery tile itself. A monastery with a monk scores like a normal cloister – choose \"Cloister\" then.",
  "monasteryEventLabel": "{name}: abbot +{points}",
  "rulesMonasteries": "• Monasteries from the expansion: remove the base-game cloisters and shuffle the new tiles into the stack.\n• After placing the tile you may deploy a meeple as a monk (scores like a normal cloister, 9 pts when completed) or as an abbot (laid on its side).\n• The abbot stays on the tile until the end of the game and only then scores: 1 pt for each tile in the monastery row and column plus 1 pt for the monastery itself.\n• An empty space stops the count in that direction.",
