  "aboutDisclaimer": "An unofficial fan-made app. Carcassonne is a trademark of its owners. All icons in the app are original.",
  "aboutLicenses": "Library licenses",
  "newGameChoiceBody": "Do you want to play again with the same players, or set the players up from scratch?\n\nPoints, goods and used circus tokens will be reset. Expansions stay as they are, and you can still change them before starting.",
  "newGameSamePlayers": "Same players",
  "newGameNewPlayers": "New players",
  "addMorePlayers": "You need at least two players. Add another one with the button",
  "expGermanCastles": "Castles in Germany",
  "expGermanCastlesDesc": "Double-size German castle tiles. The lord of a castle gets 12 pts for a completed castle, and each castle at the end of a completed road or city gives the majority players 3 extra pts.",
  "expGermanCathedrals": "Cathedrals in Germany",
  "expGermanCathedralsDesc": "Tiles with German cathedrals in the fields. A highwayman on a road to a cathedral gets double points per road segment, even for a road left unfinished at the end of the game, and the archbishop 1 pt per road segment, but only when all the roads are closed.",
  "scGermanCastle": "German castle",
  "scArchbishop": "Archbishop",
  "germanCastlesAtFeature": "German castles at the feature",
  "germanCastlesAtFeatureHint": "Set the number of German castles at the ends of the completed feature: for each one the majority players get {points} extra pts, whether or not the castle is occupied. The bonus is added after the cathedral and inn modifiers. A road that starts and ends on the same castle counts it once.",
  "roadToCathedral": "Leads to a cathedral",
  "roadToCathedralHint": "Check it if the road starts or ends on a German cathedral tile (highwayman): it scores double, that is 2 pts per tile (3 with an inn), even when it is unfinished at the end of the game.",
  "completedRoad": "Is it completed",
  "completedGermanCastle": "Is it completed",
  "germanCastleHint": "Check it if the castle is surrounded on all sides: the lord of the castle gets {completed} pts. Leave it unchecked when scoring at the end of the game: {base} pts for the castle tile and 1 pt for each surrounding tile.",
  "tilesAroundCastle": "Tiles around the castle",
  "archbishopRoadTiles": "Road segments at the cathedral",
  "archbishopInnHint": "Check it if the roads have an inn: the archbishop gets 2 pts per segment instead of 1.",
  "rulesGermanCastles": "• Each player gets 1 castle (2 with 2–3 players). You place it instead of drawing a tile; it may not touch other castles, even diagonally.\n• Lord of the castle: a completed castle (surrounded like a cloister) gives 12 pts. At the end of the game an unfinished one gives 2 pts for the castle tile and 1 pt for each surrounding tile.\n• A completed road or city with a castle at its end gives the majority players 3 pts per castle, even an unoccupied one. The bonus is added after the inn and cathedral modifiers.",
  "rulesGermanCathedrals": "• 6 tiles with cathedrals in the fields, with 3 or 4 roads from the cathedral.\n• Highwayman on a road to a cathedral: double points per segment, that is 2 pts per tile (3 with an inn). This also applies to a road unfinished at the end of the game (0 with an inn).\n• Archbishop on the cathedral scores only when all the roads from the cathedral are closed: 1 pt per road segment (2 with an inn), each segment on the cathedral tile separately. If any road stays open until the end of the game, the archbishop gets nothing."
}
